on the future  and what we need to do after brexit that  the party is looking for somebody who's  more in the here and now and that means  I've decided to withdraw from the race  and I'm going to find the way to advance  the arguments and the values that I care  about that we should support free  enterprise and the free society that we  need to be open and outward looking an  optimistic as a party as a country and  I'll find I'll find other ways to to  advance those arguments now looked to  that and talked to all the candidates  before making a decision about who else  to support well you met with mr. subject  Javid yesterday didn't you and had a  private conversation are you going to  back such a Java doll you haven't  decided I'm going to make an  announcement about what next in the in  the coming days I've spoken to lots of  the different candidates and I can see  merit in lots of them you know  ultimately I put myself forward as the  candidate of the future I've been making  arguments about what the party needs to  be like the values we need to have the  policies we need to have the tone and  the way that we talk and how we need to  be in touch with modern Britain and  appealing to younger voters and and I'm  going to be looking to see which  candidates what the candidates say and  how best to advance these arguments  within the conservative party and  ultimately within the government and the  comeback but ultimately if you've got  mr. Johnson in the final two as the  here-and-now candidate as you put it the  other two in that bracket at the top are  mr. Gav and mr. hunt both here and now  candidates to you Sajid Javid Rory Co  you'll all the change candidates isn't  it that where your heart is in terms of  trying to get one of you three into the  final two and if it ain't going to be  you surely you would back mr. Javid or  are you going to go from Mr Gove because  you want another job in government well  I'm going to look at the I'm going to  talk to the candidates and I'm going to  work out what is the best way to advance  the values that I care about in in  government in the next government under  the next prime minister  so I'll be thinking about  over the weekend what about mr. Johnson  well as I say I'm going to talk to all  of the candidates and work out what is  the best way to advance the values that  I care about in the next conservative  government well you disappointed to come  in with 20 just ahead of Rory steward  did it mate you just think I've lost  momentum this is going to get  embarrassing if I carry on is that yeah  I did I did better than than we expected  and I was really pleased with the level  of support but it's also clear that you  know making the argument for being the  candidate for the future is just is not  where the party is at the moment and  that's understandable because of the  unique circumstances that we face  following that logic the other  candidates of the future mr. Stewart  then mr. Javid both with about the same  voice that you had done actually mr.  robb as well do you reckon they should  just sort of pull out and let the big  beasts fight it out well they'll make  their decisions what do you think well  I'm not going to put pressure on them  I'm going to think about what is the  best way for me to advance the values  that I care about that I've articulated  and made the case for in this campaign  and as I say I feel like I've been  winning arguments during the campaign  and you know trying to make the argument  that this contest needs to be as open as  possible I called for TV debates we're  now having TV debates I called for the  whole future of the Conservative  government to be more pro-business and  Pro enterprise and all the other  candidates are coming to that I I said  that we can't have four occation of  parliament as a way to get through  brexit and now increasingly the  candidates are saying that too and that  just on mr. Johnson he apparently has  privately told the ERG that he would be  open to perogy empowerment he certainly  hasn't publicly ruled that out is that a  red line for you in terms of backing him  well I think that prorogue in Parliament  is would be wrong it really again stall  the the democratic ideals that we stand  for as a country and also to be totally  impractical and it would never work so  that's a so I'm clear where I stand on  that and I want us to deliver brexit and  then move forward and it's the move  for word that I've been really focused  on just in terms of the race just one  more thing in terms of all of the  candidates wouldn't it be good to have  the future of the conservative party in  this race in the final two as well given  that mr. Johnson looks like he's  unassailable now wouldn't it be good to  have someone that isn't you know one of  the old faces of the party in the final  two that's where you're at well that's  the case that I've made and you know if  you look at the results of the first  round the party is it's pretty clear  that they want somebody who's involved  in the debates of the here-and-now now  I'm going to make I'm gonna focus on the  future and I'm going to concentrate on  making sure this party is always looking  with optimism to the future to deliver  for people because that's what we need  to do that's the whole point of being in  politics is to make life better for  people in this country and that's the  values I'm going to concentrate on

